  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\nTargets nested in generic types (#362, closes #337). A target registered open inside a generic type, such as typeof(Outer<>.Inner), got an imposter that referred to the containing type's type parameters without declaring them (CS0246). The imposter now declares them, outermost first, followed by the target's own type parameters, with their constraints, so Outer\\<T>.Inner\\<U> gets InnerImposter\\<T, U>. A closed registration such as typeof(Outer\\<int>.Inner) keeps its own imposter and can sit beside the open one. The generics docs cover it with an executable example.",
